  <h2>What the notes keep from collapsing</h2>
  <article class="panel turn note"><span class="status status-interpretation">note ¹ · claim</span><p><strong>Canon note:</strong> Who will not claim Adulthood remains a child; who renounces Adulthood becomes retired; who cannot attain or retain Adulthood are invalids.</p><p><strong>Function:</strong> keeps adulthood tied to declared responsibility while preserving visible categories for refusal, retirement, and incapacity.</p></article>
  <article class="panel turn note"><span class="status status-interpretation">note ² · adulthood</span><p><strong>Canon note:</strong> all adults are the same legal age, alive now.</p><p><strong>Function:</strong> resists age hierarchy among adults. Once competence is demonstrated, the adult enters the same public present.</p></article>
  <article class="panel turn note"><span class="status status-interpretation">note ³ · field standards</span><p><strong>Canon note:</strong> Each field outside the body politic will require their own set of demonstrable skills validation process delineated in a field specific interdependent way canon.</p><p><strong>Function:</strong> keeps competence domain-specific rather than pretending one demonstration proves every field.</p></article>
